WEBVTT

00:02:28.044 --> 00:02:32.044
without triggering any of the three 
catastrophic failures.

00:02:32.044 --> 00:02:34.274
Which thrusters should you activate?

00:02:34.274 --> 00:02:36.535
Answer in 3

00:02:36.535 --> 00:02:39.524
Answer in 2

00:02:39.524 --> 00:02:42.224
Answer in 1

00:02:42.224 --> 00:02:44.382
The most important thing 
to remember here

00:02:44.382 --> 00:02:47.342
is that even if we know 
that one thing causes another,

00:02:47.342 --> 00:02:50.382
the converse is not necessarily true.

00:02:50.382 --> 00:02:54.449
For example, this panic switch 
shuts off the coil runner’s engine.

00:02:54.449 --> 00:02:57.909
But the engine being off 
doesn’t necessarily mean

00:02:57.909 --> 00:02:59.839
the panic switch was engaged—

00:02:59.839 --> 00:03:02.619
the coil runner could be 
out of fuel, or damaged—